# arch-bootstrap

Interactive post-install setup for Arch Linux. Not a disk installer.

    ./bootstrap.sh -n      # dry run first
    ./bootstrap.sh         # the real thing

Run as a normal user with sudo, not root.

Flags: -p NAME profile · -n dry run · -y non-interactive (needs -p) · -l list · -h help.
Env: GIT_NAME, GIT_EMAIL.

Profiles: minimal (CLI), lightweight (i3 + zram), dev (toolchains + docker).

Steps: upgrade, packages, aur, dotfiles, services, zram, git.
With -y all steps run, but zram only if the profile sets ZRAM=1.

